      "message": "`slugify` now transliterates accented letters, so `café` becomes `cafe`. All 3 tests in `tests/test_core.py` pass.\n\nThe bug was in the `elif ch.isalpha(): continue` branch, which silently dropped any non-ASCII letter. In `slug/core.py`, each character is now decomposed with NFKD and stripped to ASCII, so `é` becomes `e`, `ü` becomes `u`, and so on. A small lookup table covers letters that don't decompose, such as `ß` → `ss`, `æ` → `ae`, `ø` → `o`, and `ł` → `l`.\n\nI also added one regression test, `test_accented_letters_are_transliterated`, covering `café` and `Ünïcödé Straße`. You didn't ask for it, so drop it if you'd rather not keep it.\n\nTwo behaviours to be aware of:\n- Letters with no ASCII form, such as CJK characters, are still dropped, as before.\n- NFKD also maps some non-letter characters, so `²` now becomes `2` instead of a dash.",
